# Civ term capitalization

In **player-facing text** (chat, GUI lore/titles, quest YAML, commands, admin messages, PRDs/issues) and **documentation about gameplay**, capitalize established CivCraft domain terms. Do not change Java identifiers, config keys, or file paths unless you are editing display strings.

## Always capitalize (common terms)

| Term | Notes |
|------|--------|
| **Civilization** / **Civ** | Game entity; not generic “civilization” in historical prose |
| **Town** | Player settlement |
| **City-State** | Hyphenated when used as the game concept |
| **Resident** | Player account / member |
| **Town Hall** | Seat of a Town; often the first structure in a new City-State |
| **Capital** | A Town that is the seat of a Civilization (not generic “capital city” in history text) |
| **Capitol** | The capitol Town or its Capitol structure when the game uses that spelling |
| **Civics** | Civic research / unlock tree (`civics.yml`), not generic “civics lesson” |
| **Structure** / **Wonder** | Buildables when referring to game objects |
| **Culture** | Claim/border system |
| **Policies** | Town or civ policy picks when referring to game systems |
| **Hammers**, **Growth**, **Beakers** | Core town yields |
| **SpawnEmpire** | Proper name of the spawn civ/town |
| **Imperial Advisor** | Guide NPC |
| **Backpack**, **Civ Manager** | UI systems |
| **WarTime** | Scheduled conflict window |

Use existing in-game spellings from nearby copy (`Found City-State`, `Shady Merchant`, structure display names from config) before inventing new casing.

## Examples

```yaml
# ❌ BAD
lore:
  - "Join a civilization and build a town hall."

# ✅ GOOD
lore:
  - "Join a Civilization and build a Town Hall."
```

```java
// ❌ BAD
CivMessage.send(resident, "Your town needs more hammers.");

// ✅ GOOD
CivMessage.send(resident, "Your Town needs more Hammers.");
```

## When unsure

If a word might be a Civ term (e.g. **Civic** vs **Civics**, **Dungeon**, **Marketplace** as a structure name), **ask the user** once rather than guessing lowercase or over-capitalizing generic English. **Do not** leave **Capital**, **Capitol**, or **Civics** lowercase in player-facing copy when they refer to game concepts.

## Exceptions

- Ordinary English where the word is not the game concept (“walk from spawn”, “world map link”).
- Third-party or Mojang terms (Minecraft, Shift key).
- Code/API names follow Java/YAML conventions (`town`, `getTown()`).
